# /etc/aishie/aishie.env: the operator's settings of this server's AIshie
# stack. setup-server.sh writes it once, from its arguments, and never again:
# edit it by hand. Nothing in it is secret; it is root's (0600) all the same.
#
# One NAME=value per line: no export, no comment after a value, and no quotes
# but FRAME_ANCESTORS's (below). compose.yaml reads it, and so do
# aishie-update and aishie, which take each value as it is written.

# This server's DNS name. https://HOST is where people, agents and the
# runtime reach AIshie, and Caddy gets its certificate for it once the name
# points at this server. After a change: aishie compose up -d (Core, the
# runtime and Caddy take the new name).
HOST=test.aishie.app

# edge or stable. On stable a channel must be a release, X.Y.Z, and
# aishie-update refuses anything else. A server set up before they had these
# names says staging or production, which aishie-update takes as edge and
# stable until a later release: change it by hand.
ENVIRONMENT=edge

# The channel each image follows. aishie-update, every five minutes, pulls
# the channel's tag and deploys the image it names whenever that changes.
# Edge follows :edge, main's tip once its checks have passed; stable follows
# a release, X.Y.Z, and is upgraded by changing it here (README.md, Upgrading
# stable). Each must be an image of its own repository, by tag or by
# digest.
CORE_IMAGE=ghcr.io/aishie-education/aishie-core:edge
RUNTIME_IMAGE=ghcr.io/aishie-education/aishie-agent-runtime:edge
WEB_IMAGE=ghcr.io/aishie-education/aishie-frontend:edge

# The stack's network: a subnet no other network on this server uses, and
# Caddy's address in it, which is the one proxy Core trusts. To change them,
# change both, then: aishie compose down && aishie compose up -d (the images
# stay the ones deployed; the data is in volumes and stays too).
AISHIE_SUBNET=172.30.83.0/24
AISHIE_CADDY_IP=172.30.83.10

# How long Docker gives the runtime to stop before it kills it: its
# SHUTDOWN_GRACE (runtime.env, 15s by default) and 15 seconds more.
RUNTIME_STOP_GRACE=30s

# Optional: which other sites may show AIshie in a frame, such as an LMS that
# opens it in an iframe (README.md, Frames). It is the web image's
# Content-Security-Policy frame-ancestors, sources separated by spaces and
# written as CSP writes them. Unset (or empty), only AIshie's own pages may
# frame it: 'self'. It is the one value in this file that takes quotes,
# double quotes around the whole value, because CSP's keywords carry single
# quotes of their own and Docker would otherwise cut the value at the first
# one. For example:
#   FRAME_ANCESTORS="'self' https://canvas.example.edu"   AIshie, and that LMS
#   FRAME_ANCESTORS="'none'"                              no page at all
# A value on more than one line stops the web from starting, and so its next
# update is rolled back. A site that frames AIshie from another domain also
# needs COOKIE_SAMESITE=none in core.env, or nobody stays signed in inside
# the frame. After a change: aishie compose up -d web
# FRAME_ANCESTORS="'self'"

# Optional: what stands in front of this server. Unset (or empty), nothing
# does: people reach Caddy at this server's own address, and Caddy takes a
# client's address from the connection. cloudflare: the name's DNS record is
# proxied by Cloudflare (the orange cloud), for people who cannot reach this
# server's own address, as in mainland China when it is blocked there
# (README.md, Behind Cloudflare). Caddy then takes the visitor's address
# from Cloudflare's CF-Connecting-IP, on connections from Cloudflare's own
# addresses alone (fetched from Cloudflare every week, the last list kept
# when a fetch fails), and gives it to Core and the runtime in
# X-Forwarded-For. Its certificate comes by HTTP-01 through Cloudflare. After
# a change: aishie front-proxy (setup-server.sh, run again, does the same).
# FRONT_PROXY=cloudflare
# With FRONT_PROXY, yes refuses (403) a request that comes neither from the
# front proxy's addresses nor from a private one (the stack's own network,
# where the runtime reaches Core): nobody reaches the site past Cloudflare.
# Unset (or no), people may reach this server's own address too. After a
# change: aishie front-proxy
# FRONT_PROXY_ONLY=yes
